<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Ayyubid Emirate of Damascus</h1><p class="st-meta">1193 CE – 1260 CE · capital Damascus</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Ayyubid principality of Damascus after Saladin, a prize fought over by his brothers, sons and grandsons until the Mongols arrived in 1260.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a> died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> in 1193, his empire was divided among his sons, and Damascus went to the eldest, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-afdal">al-Afdal</a> Ali. In 1196 his uncle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-adil">al-Adil</a> and brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-aziz">al-Aziz</a> drove him out, and Damascus passed to al-Adil's line.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> was the richest prize in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-arab-republic">Syria</a> and the seat of a scholarly and religious elite. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-muazzam-isa">Al-Mu'azzam Isa</a> (1218-1227), a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanafi-school">Hanafi</a> jurist, built schools and dismantled the walls of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> in 1219 to keep them from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states">Crusaders</a>. Later princes, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-nasir-dawud">al-Nasir Dawud</a>, al-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-ashraf-musa-sultan-of-damascus">Ashraf Musa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/as-salih-ismail">al-Salih Ismail</a>, fought the sultans in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>; al-<a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/salihids">Salih</a> Ismail even ceded castles to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/franks">Franks</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/as-salih-ayyub">Al-Salih Ayyub</a> took the city in 1245.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-nasir-yusuf">Al-Nasir Yusuf</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ayyubid-emirate-of-aleppo">Ayyubid Emirate of Aleppo</a> seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> in 1250. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> occupied it in March 1260, and after their defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ain-jalut">Ain Jalut</a> it passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluks</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="emirate, 1193 CE – 1260 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">emirate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:83.44%;width:1.33%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1193 CE – 1260 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Damascus</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>al-Afdal Ali, al-Mu'azzam Isa, al-Salih Ismail</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/syria">Syria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ayyubids of Damascus</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1226&amp;focus=ayyubid-emirate-of-damascus" aria-label="Ayyubid Emirate of Damascus on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5607 962 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ayyubid Emirate of Damascus lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5927 1218L5811 1337M5927 1218L7559 780"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5811 1337h0M7559 780h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M592